        "id": "scene_b2_u03_1",
        "desc": "The bank of the Word Pond is full of flapping brown hens with red combs — ten of them — running in every direction with feathers flying. A butterfly net with a wooden handle lies on the sand; high above, a white jet plane draws a vapor trail across the sky. Bun points at the net; Pip, trying to say the word, has shouted it backwards and now stares at all the hens that came running; Hedgie covers his head; Beads peeks from a lily pad. Hidden in the picture: the net, a hen, ten hens, the jet. Grumble does NOT appear.",
